{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof needs two normalization lemmas: `fderiv_apply` converts differentiation of a scalar field component to component evaluation after differentiating the vector field, and the mixed derivative must use the existing `space_deriv_time_deriv_commute` lemma (the attempted reverse-name identifier does not exist). After expanding the derivative rules, Faraday’s identity and differentiated Gauss law close the result algebraically.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  have hmax :=\\n    (isExtrema_iff_gauss_ampere_magneticFieldMatrix hA J hJ).mp h\\n  have hamp :\\n      (fun s => ∂ₜ (A.electricField 𝓕.c · x i) s) =\\n        fun s =>\\n          1 / (𝓕.μ₀ * 𝓕.ε₀) *\\n              ∑ j, ∂[j] (A.magneticFieldMatrix 𝓕.c s · (j, i)) x -\\n            (1 / 𝓕.ε₀) * J.currentDensity 𝓕.c s x i := by\\n    funext s\\n    simpa (disch := fun_prop) [Time.deriv, fderiv_apply] using\\n      time_deriv_electricField_of_isExtrema hA J hJ h s x i\\n  have hamp' := congrArg (fun f : Time → ℝ => ∂ₜ f t) hamp\\n  have hgauss :\\n      (fun y => ∑ j, ∂[j] (A.electricField 𝓕.c t · j) y) =\\n        fun y => J.chargeDensity 𝓕.c t y / 𝓕.ε₀ := by\\n    funext y\\n    simpa [Space.div] using (hmax t y).1\\n  have hgauss' := congrArg (fun f : Space d → ℝ => ∂[i] f x) hgauss\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n      [Time.deriv, Space.deriv_eq_fderiv_basis, fderiv_apply,\\n        fderiv_fun_sub, fderiv_const_mul, fderiv_fun_sum,\\n        space_deriv_time_deriv_commute,\\n        time_deriv_magneticFieldMatrix A (hA.of_le (ENat.LEInfty.out)),\\n        Space.deriv_commute, Finset.sum_sub_distrib] at hamp' hgauss'\\n  linear_combination (norm := field_simp [FreeSpace.c_sq]) hamp' -\\n    (𝓕.c ^ 2) * hgauss'\"}"}}
